{"availability":"available","full":"nickjmorrow/ranked-choice","name":"ranked-choice","description":"Create, vote, and simulate polls that use the ranked choice voting algorithm.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2020-06-23T01:37:10Z","updated":"2026-09-24T17:52:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://ranked-choice.netlify.app/","topics":["demo","voting"],"demo":"https://ranked-choice.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.742Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.742Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.742Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.742Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Polls you answer by ranking, counted by instant runoff — with a results page that shows the count happen, round by round, instead of only announcing who won.","Live demo: ranked-choice.204-168-227-216.sslip.io — open the example poll's results and press Replay the count to watch Kyoto overtake Lisbon on transferred votes. No sign-in. The example poll resets every night; polls you create are kept for 30 days.","I built this because I wanted a simple way to run a ranked-choice poll and could not find one I liked. A ranked ballot lets you vote for your favourite without wasting your vote: if it cannot win, your ballot moves to your next choice. That is easy to say and hard to trust, so I made the results the whole count rather than a winner — the votes each option had in each round, which were first choices and which arrived by transfer, who was eliminated and why, and how many ballots ran out of choices along the way."],"features":["Vote on the example poll,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nickjmorrow/ranked-choice/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"83dc60445d60afdd6344c968e5286b5289e3bc33d956eb8e327a391d956e677a","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.925Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:09:13.925Z","projectIn